/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Explanation of why the above SELECT statement cannot be used: The SELECT statement above has two columns specified \(Customer and SUM\(OrderPrice\). The "SUM\(OrderPrice\)" returns a single value \(that is the total sum of the "OrderPrice" column\), while "Customer" returns 6 values \(one value for each row in the "Orders" table\). This will therefore not give us the correct result. However, you have seen that the GROUP BY statement solves this problem.)
/E (Explanation of why the above SELECT statement cannot be used: The SELECT statement above has two columns specified \(Customer and SUM\(OrderPrice\). The "SUM\(OrderPrice\)" returns a single value \(that is the total sum of the "OrderPrice" column\), while "Customer" returns 6 values \(one value for each row in the "Orders" table\). This will therefore not give us the correct result. However, you have seen that the GROUP BY statement solves this problem.)
/Pg 145 0 R
/K [28]
>>
